Data source (the PVPC provider, the only one today): Red Eléctrica de
España, S.A.U. (REE), part of Redeia.

The electricity prices this plugin shows (PVPC 2.0TD, indicator 1001) are
published by Red Eléctrica de España through its REData API
(https://apidatos.ree.es) and, optionally, its ESIOS system
(https://api.esios.ree.es). They belong to REE and are not covered by this
plugin's licence.

REE's legal notice (https://www.ree.es/es/aviso-legal) allows their use for
informative, non-commercial purposes provided that the user:
  I.   names Red Eléctrica clearly and explicitly as the source of the data;
  II.  does not alter or distort the meaning of the data;
  III. gives the date of the data's last update;
  IV.  does not use REE's logos, trademarks or distinctive signs.

This plugin does so: its widgets show "Red Eléctrica" with the date and time
of REE's last update ("Red Eléctrica · 24 nov 20:46") wherever there is room,
its alerts name "REE" as their source, prices are shown as published (only
converted from €/MWh to €/kWh), and no REE logo is used.

The test fixtures in src/fixtures are answers of the REData and ESIOS APIs
saved on 24 November 2026, kept to test the parser; the demo data in
src/demo.ts reuses two of those days' hourly prices.

Kiosko and this plugin are not affiliated with, nor endorsed by, Red
Eléctrica de España.
